  "worked_solution": "Notice that if we substitute $x=0$ into the given equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{x}^{2}-x+k \\\\ y & =-(0)^{2}-(0)+k \\\\ y & =k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nmeaning that the curve intercepts the $y$-axis at the point $(0,k).$ Based on the graph, we see that we must have $k=3$ since our parabola intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,3).$",
